From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "amcsc: do not limit 8bit HDR output"

This reverts common_drivers commit d9ec1b3b91822e03fdbeb09305aa0f63fbbb4c17
(author: Portisch <hugo.portisch@yahoo.de>), so that the files our 0001-0022 patch
stack edits stay byte-identical to f9af0b41 while the package pin moves
to cc0e6659. Applied before 0001; the 9 reverts run newest first.
See docs/release_update_survey_ce_20261121.md section 2.2.

---
diff --git a/drivers/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c b/drivers/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c
index f75f73a0b..e0963e519 100644
--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ static uint pre_gamut_conv_en;
 signed int vd1_contrast_offset;
 
 signed int saturation_offset;
-bool limit_8bit_hdr10 = false;
+bool limit_8bit_hdr10 = true;
 
 #ifndef CONFIG_AMLOGIC_ZAPPER_CUT
 static bool cur_hdmi_out_fmt;
